        "title": "‘Shortcuts Playground’ lets you create shortcuts using natural langauge",
        "url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/05/21/shortcuts-playground-lets-you-create-shortcuts-using-natural-langauge/",
        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2025/10/shortcuts-ios-26.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p>Federico Viticci at <em>MacStories</em> is <a href=\"https://www.macstories.net/stories/introducing-shortcuts-playground/\">out today with yet another wild tool</a> that integrates with Apple’s Shortcuts app.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Shortcuts Playground from Federico is a plugin for Claude Code and Codex that can “create any shortcut for Apple’s Shortcuts app using natural language.”</p>\n\n\n\n <a data-layer-pagetype=\"post\" data-layer-postcategory=\"shortcuts\" data-layer-viewtype=\"unknown\" data-post-id=\"1052955\" href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/05/21/shortcuts-playground-lets-you-create-shortcuts-using-natural-langauge/#more-1052955\" class=\"more-link\">more…</a>",
