        "url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/05/21/strava-adds-dedicated-strength-training-support-for-sets-reps-weight-and-muscle-groups/",
        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/05/strava-strenght.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p>Strava is completely overhauling its strength training experience, with a new workout log, automatic muscle maps, new sharing tools, and expanded integrations with apps and devices. Here are the details.</p>\n\n\n\n <a data-layer-pagetype=\"post\" data-layer-postcategory=\"strava\" data-layer-viewtype=\"unknown\" data-post-id=\"1052968\" href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/05/21/strava-adds-dedicated-strength-training-support-for-sets-reps-weight-and-muscle-groups/#more-1052968\" class=\"more-link\">more…</a>",
        "type": "Technology",
